# island.is patch — Next 16 Pages Router SSR does not pass the CSP nonce to React
# 19's streaming renderer, so streamed Suspense boundary scripts ($RC/$RB, e.g. from
# island-ui's lazy-loaded icons) come out un-nonced, get CSP-blocked, and break SSR
# with React error #419. This ports what App Router already does (fizzOptions.nonce)
# into the Pages Router: it passes `streamOptions: { nonce }` to the Fizz call.
#
# Patched in all four precompiled pages runtimes (this is what actually runs — the
# readable dist/server/render.js is NOT loaded at runtime, in dev or prod):
#   - pages.runtime.prod.js        (webpack, production)
#   - pages-turbo.runtime.prod.js  (turbopack, production)
#   - pages.runtime.dev.js         (webpack, local dev)
#   - pages-turbo.runtime.dev.js   (turbopack, local dev)
#
# Upstream issue: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/96443
# Upstream fix:   https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/96447
# -> Drop this patch once #96447 is merged and we bump Next past it.
